A||N||1||DaRkLoRD||opinions on painting idea||||1||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||03-23-2000||06:57 PM||||Yesterday while in the hardware store, I came across some spraypaint that said it had a suede texture. So I picked it up, and felt the lid.. it wasn't exactly suede of course, but it was pretty cool!<P>Anyway, that got me thinking about an idea for a painting technique for a Fiero. Not sure if it'd be considered "ricey" or not.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Have the car painted with a high gloss paint (most people's cars are done like this anyway) and then mask of a section (like a stencil) in the shape of a Pegasus or whatever you want, and then spray the exact same color, except flat instead of glossy. When the clearcoat is applied, the flat color section wouldn't be extremely visible, but it might look interesting..<P>I doubt I'd do this mod myself, as I prefer to go for a very minimalist look.. small pontiac badge on the front.. GT on the quarter windows and *maybe* something small about the engine on the fenders (like the cavaliers say 3.1 EFI) but I know some people like the look of this stuff, so I just thought I'd share the idea.<P>comments?||||reg||1
Z||000001||sdm1964||03-23-2000||09:30 PM||||Lord, i am like you , i think less is more. My GT has no stickers or decals any where on the car. Black, white and mine!!! I like to watch people try to look at the car as i fly by them trying to wonder what just flashed past them. I had this lady in atlanta almost break her neck trying to figure out what kinda car i was driving, I have an 84 Z28 that had the multi-color stripe at the bottom, when i had it repainted, I had them removed. Good idea, might look cool but just not for me.||||reg||12
